      "spans": [
        { "text": "The window is frets " },
        { "text": "0–3", "marks": ["code"] },
        {
          "text": " — four frets, not five, because the nut cuts it short, as chapters 1 through 3 all said. Chapter 2 called this the friendliest shape on the neck, and that hasn't changed: seventeen dots live inside those four frets, and every fret in the window carries something."
        }
